  "findings": {
    "Prob034_dff8": "Reference initializes q=0; prompt specifies no initial value. Initial value only change passes 41 samples in both arms.",
    "Prob053_m2014_q4d": "Reference initializes out=0; prompt specifies no initial value. Initial value only change passes 100 samples in both arms. Reference becomes X after first edge in original TB; later masked comparisons do not demonstrate meaningful toggle coverage.",
    "Prob104_mt2015_muxdff": "Reference initializes Q=0; prompt specifies no initial value. Initial value only change passes 199 samples in both arms.",
    "Prob062_bugs_mux2": "Candidates preserve buggy scalar out, reinforced by harness preserve-width policy. HDLBits clean interface uses 8-bit out. Width-only change compiles but fails 111/114 samples; reference selector reversal sel?a:b also needed. Prompt broken expression suggests opposite sel?b:a and gives no explicit selector convention.",
    "Prob093_ece241_2014_q3": "Candidates match all 16 binary entries of the provided prompt K-map. At cd=11, ab=10 prompt says 1; reference mux_in[2]=~d says 0. Reference-matching change only passes 60 samples.",
    "Prob149_ece241_2013_q4": "Prompt explicitly turns supplement on if previous level was lower (rising water); candidates do that. Reference turns supplement on at intermediate levels reached from above (falling water). Reversing intermediate direction only passes 2040 samples. Official stimulus uses adjacent level transitions, so skip-level policy is not a cause of observed failures."
  },
